# Negative corpus: branch to a label bound past the end of the code.
# A past-end label is legal ONLY as a .catch 'to' target; using it as a
# branch target must fail at parse time; the .errors twin pins a substring of
# the reported error.

.class corpus/BadBranch

.method static jumpAway ()V
.regs 0
goto tail
return
tail:
.end
